<title>FRANCE: Cuban imports seen at over $2.5 bln in 96 - paper.</title>
<headline>Cuban imports seen at over $2.5 bln in 96 - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cuban imports are expected to total just over $2.5 billion this year, exports a little more than $1.5 billion, and gross tourism revenues $1.3 billion, Cuba's central bank governor said in an interview in Wednesday's edition of the Paris newspaper Le Monde.</p>
<p>&quot;I can tell you that imports are a little over $2.5 billion, exports a little more than $1.5 billion and gross tourism revenues will reach $1.3 billion this year,&quot; Francisco Soberon told Le Monde.</p>
<p>He gave no comparative year-earlier figures.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
